#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Phase 8 (ADR D17): JsonRpc's generalization beyond one in-flight
⍝ Call — pipelined Send/AwaitResponse with out-of-order arrival,
⍝ CallBatch, and notification dispatch (registered handler vs.
⍝ backward-compatible fallthrough to h.Notifications) — plus Mcp's
⍝ 'notifications/tools/list_changed' reaction. Against
⍝ examples/toy-jsonrpc-pipeline-server.py, purpose-built for this (see
⍝ its docstring for why neither existing toy server can be made to
⍝ answer out of order or in batch on demand).
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Shell.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpc.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Mcp.dyalog'

cmd←'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-pipeline-server.py'
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
h.Timeout←10

⍝ --- Pipelined Send/AwaitResponse: a fast request fired SECOND must
⍝ be collectable BEFORE a slow one fired FIRST resolves ---
t0←⎕AI[3]
slowId←h JsonRpc.Send('delay'(seconds:2 ⋄ text:'slow'))
fastId←h JsonRpc.Send('echo'(text:'fast'))
fastResp←h JsonRpc.AwaitResponse fastId
fastElapsed←⎕AI[3]-t0
⎕←'fast response -> ',fastResp.result,' (',(⍕fastElapsed),'ms after send)'
⎕←'fast arrived well before slow''s 2000ms delay: ',⍕fastElapsed<1500

slowResp←h JsonRpc.AwaitResponse slowId
⎕←'slow response -> ',slowResp.result

⍝ Call is unchanged: Send then immediately AwaitResponse on that id.
r←h JsonRpc.Call('echo'(text:'plain call'))
⎕←'plain call -> ',r.result

⍝ --- CallBatch: one JSON-RPC batch message; the server replies with
⍝ its responses deliberately REVERSED from request order, so getting
⍝ argsVec's own order back proves CallBatch reorders by id, not by
⍝ arrival order ---
batchArgs←('echo'(text:'one'))('echo'(text:'two'))('echo'(text:'three'))
batchResps←h JsonRpc.CallBatch batchArgs
⎕←'batch results in argsVec order: ',⍕batchResps.result

⍝ --- Notification dispatch: a registered handler fires, AND the
⍝ notification is still queued in h.Notifications either way (ADR
⍝ D17: "as well as", not "instead of" — backward compatible) ---
_TestHandlerLog←⍬
⎕FX'{r}←h _TestNotifyHandler notif' '#._TestHandlerLog,←⊂notif' 'r←⍬'
h JsonRpc.OnNotification('custom/registered' '#._TestNotifyHandler')

r←h JsonRpc.Call('notify'(method:'custom/registered' ⋄ notifyParams:(x:1)))
⎕←'notify(registered) ack -> ',r.result
⎕←'handler fired exactly once: ',⍕1=≢_TestHandlerLog
⎕←'handler saw method: ',(⊃_TestHandlerLog).method
⎕←'also queued in Notifications (as well as, not instead): ',⍕∨/'custom/registered'∘≡¨h.Notifications.method

⍝ A notification with NO registered handler must still fall through
⍝ to h.Notifications exactly as v1 did (backward compatibility).
before←≢h.Notifications
r←h JsonRpc.Call('notify'(method:'custom/unregistered' ⋄ notifyParams:(y:2)))
⎕←'notify(unregistered) ack -> ',r.result
⎕←'unregistered notification queued: ',⍕(≢h.Notifications)>before
⎕←'unregistered notification did NOT invoke the registered handler: ',⍕1=≢_TestHandlerLog

JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⍝ --- Mcp's notifications/tools/list_changed reaction ---
h2←() Mcp.Connect cmd
⎕←'mcp connected to ',h2.ServerInfo.name
⎕←'ToolsStale initially 0: ',⍕0=h2.JsonRpc.ToolsStale
{}Mcp.ListTools h2
⎕←'ToolsStale still 0 after an ordinary ListTools: ',⍕0=h2.JsonRpc.ToolsStale

r←h2.JsonRpc JsonRpc.Call('notify'(method:'notifications/tools/list_changed' ⋄ notifyParams:()))
⎕←'server announced list_changed -> ',r.result
⎕←'ToolsStale now 1: ',⍕1=h2.JsonRpc.ToolsStale
{}Mcp.ListTools h2
⎕←'ToolsStale cleared by the next ListTools fetch: ',⍕0=h2.JsonRpc.ToolsStale

Mcp.Disconnect h2
⎕←'done'
⎕OFF
